    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with three primary offensive engines in the lineup: **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90). **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Mickey Moniak** benefit immensely from favorable matchups against Rhett Lowder and Nick Martinez, respectively; both pairings see significant boosts from the SP skill factors and park environment. **Seiya Suzuki** remains a high-floor play against Eric Lauer, where his platoon advantage and batting order position at the top of the lineup solidify his elite status. While **Corbin Carroll** (68.61) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.30) provide strong secondary production, our aggressive pursuit of the scarce stolen base category makes **Corbin Carroll** a locked starter despite a challenging matchup against Casey Mize, as his capacity to impact the basepaths remains our highest priority.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Travis Bazzana** (42.07) on the bench. He was the closest to cracking the active roster, but his score was suppressed by a matchup against Christian Scott and a lack of confirmed lineup data, which penalized his projection versus the more stable, high-upside profiles of **Max Muncy** (61.70) and **Jose Caballero** (50.70). We remain cautious regarding **Austin Riley** (52.51); while he clears the floor, the 33% rain risk in his matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez warrants monitoring. We are also tracking **Gabriel Moreno** (54.60) and **Josh Naylor** (47.41) closely, as their scores are currently tied to assumed batting order positions. If any late-breaking lineup news shifts them out of their expected slots, their efficiency scores\u2014already hovering near the marginal threshold\u2014could necessitate a shift to bench reserves like **Cole Young** or **Zach McKinstry** to protect our game caps.",
